cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DilutionAttention, please cite this software."
title: "DilutionAttention: a parameter-free attention operator that divides each bid by the demand its key has already absorbed"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Royer
    given-names: Nick
    affiliation: "Royer Research Labs, LLC"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Royer-Research-Labs/Dilution-Attention"
abstract: >-
  DilutionAttention is a causal attention operator with no learnable parameters: each query's
  softmax bid on a key is divided by the cumulative demand that key has already received from
  earlier queries, and the shares are renormalised. The release contains the operator, fused
  Triton kernels with exact gradients, training and evaluation code, run records for 200+
  training runs, and an evidence ledger. At 209M parameters with no position encoding, dilution
  models retrieve planted keywords at eight times their training context, where matched softmax
  controls fall to chance; within the trained context, loss and sample quality track softmax
  with RoPE.
keywords:
  - attention
  - transformer
  - language model
  - length extrapolation
  - long context
  - position encoding
